 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519591,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the cost of financing for a 30-year mortgage of $108,993 with 6.14% interest if the mortgage is paid off?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In the previous exercise, you found the monthly payment was $663.32.</p>\n<p>The total paid, <i>T</i>, on a <i>t</i> year mortgage with monthly payments <i>pmt</i> is <i><span data-math=\"T = pmt \\times 12 \\times t\"></span></i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"T = {\\text{ }}663.32{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}12{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}20{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}\\$238,795.20\"></span></p>\n<p>The total paid is $238,795.20.</p>\n<p>Subtract the cost of the house from the total paid to find the cost of financing.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"238,795.20{\\text{ }}-{\\text{ }}108,993{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}\\$129,802.20\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$129,802.20"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
